🔹 1. Data Extraction from Mainframe (VSAM / PS Files)

We worked with VSAM and flat files containing data in EBCDIC format, which is not directly readable in modern systems.

👉 Work done:

Extracted raw data from mainframe datasets
Handled different file structures and record formats
Ensured data integrity during extraction

⚠️ Challenges:

EBCDIC data is not human-readable
Different file layouts caused inconsistencies
Large file sizes required optimized processing
🔹 2. EBCDIC to Readable Format Conversion

The core task was converting binary EBCDIC data into meaningful readable data.

👉 Work done:

Used COBOL programs to decode EBCDIC data
Applied COPYBOOK mapping to interpret data fields
Converted raw bytes into structured records

⚠️ Challenges:

Incorrect mapping could corrupt entire data
Handling special characters and encoding issues
Maintaining accuracy across multiple files
🔹 3. COBOL & Copybook-Based Data Mapping

COPYBOOKs were used to define the structure of data.

👉 Work done:

Analyzed COPYBOOK layouts
Mapped fields to corresponding database columns
Ensured correct data types and field lengths

⚠️ Challenges:

Complex nested structures in COPYBOOKs
Misalignment of fields caused incorrect output
Required deep understanding of legacy systems
🔹 4. Java-Based Tool Development (Frontend + Integration)

A Java-based tool was developed to manage the entire process.

👉 Work done:

Built UI for uploading files and triggering jobs
Integrated Java with COBOL backend
Automated data flow from mainframe to database

⚠️ Challenges:

Integration between old (COBOL) and modern (Java) systems
Handling errors during runtime
Ensuring smooth communication between components
🔹 5. Data Loading into SQL Server (ETL Process)

After transformation, data was loaded into SQL Server tables.

👉 Work done:

Designed SQL tables based on COPYBOOK structure
Automated data insertion using Java
Ensured consistency and validation

⚠️ Challenges:

Handling large data volume
Maintaining performance during bulk inserts
Preventing data duplication or loss
🔹 6. Multi-File Data Migration & Automation

The system handled multiple input files simultaneously.

👉 Work done:

Automated batch processing
Managed dependencies between files
Scheduled and monitored jobs

⚠️ Challenges:

File dependency issues
Processing failures in batch jobs
Ensuring complete migration without missing data
🔹 7. Testing, Debugging & Performance Optimization

Testing was critical due to the sensitivity of data.

👉 Work done:

Compared before vs after data outputs
Fixed data mismatches and errors
Optimized processing speed

⚠️ Challenges:

Identifying errors in huge datasets
Debugging legacy + modern integration issues
Reducing execution time
🔹 8. Production Support & Issue Resolution

Post-deployment support ensured system stability.

👉 Work done:

Provided real-time issue resolution
Monitored production environment
Fixed environment-related issues

⚠️ Challenges:

Differences between dev and production environments
Urgent issue handling under time pressure
Ensuring zero downtime
🎯 Final Impact (What Client Got)

✔ Converted unreadable data into structured format
✔ Automated ETL process
✔ Improved data accessibility
✔ Reduced manual effort
✔ Faster and reliable system
